# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

This resource manages [agent secrets](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/agents/secrets), separately from Actions secrets and the `copilot` Actions environment.

Fine-grained personal access tokens and GitHub Apps require repository **Agent secrets: write** permission. Classic tokens require the `repo` scope. The authenticated user must have collaborator access to the repository.

Provide either `value`, which the provider encrypts using a LibSodium-compatible sealed box, or `value_encrypted` with its `key_id`. Pre-encrypted values must use the key returned by `github_agents_public_key`, not an Actions public key. Base64 encoding alone is not encryption.

Both value attributes are sensitive, but **plaintext `value` is still stored in Terraform state**. Protect your state and supply values through secure inputs rather than hardcoding them.

External changes are detected using timestamps and restored from configuration. To keep a placeholder value in Terraform and manage subsequent rotations outside Terraform, use `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [updated_at] }`.

